# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. `dist/` is the publishable site produced by build_site.py - it is
# generated, so it is not versioned. It is published via WorkBuddy
# (scripts/publish-workbuddy.ps1 audits it, the daily automation uploads it).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private data. NEVER commit these:
#   state/  - de-duplication fingerprints, firstSeen/lastSeen and the raw
#             canonical corpus (~1 MB). Internal, and not needed by the site.
#   inbox/  - manual exports from login-walled sites (Xiaohongshu, BOSS Zhipin).
#             May contain referral codes, personal notes, contact details.
#   logs/harness-*.log - machine-local run logs (absolute paths, console noise).
#   logs/*.txt         - stdout dumps written by manual runs of run-daily.ps1
#                        (run-daily-stdout.txt, publish-*.txt, guards-*.txt).
#                        Machine-local console noise, not part of the product;
#                        the structured run history lives in logs/runs.json.
#   .tmp-verify-profile/ - throwaway Chrome profiles from verify-web.mjs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
web/data/state/
web/data/inbox/
web/data/archive/
web/data/logs/harness-*.log
web/data/logs/*.txt
.tmp-verify-profile/
.tmp-*/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. The API key belongs in an environment variable or the DSH credential
# store (~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml), never in this repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
config/*.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / Node / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Research working files.
#
# IMPORTANT - do not un-ignore research/_probe/:
#   It holds ~230 raw HTTP response bodies (7.5 MB), and a credential scan found
#   four credential-SHAPED strings (sk- + 38 chars) inside a scraped
#   lab-deepmind RSS file. They are almost certainly a false positive (an HTML
#   entity or an obfuscated URL fragment), but "almost certainly" is not good
#   enough for a public repository: nothing in there is needed to run the
#   workbench, so it stays local.
#   The conclusions that DO matter live in docs/, research/source_registry.json,
#   research/channel_probe.json and research/jobs_kb.json.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
research/_probe/
research/_scratch/
research/__pycache__/
research/channel_probe.json

# Throwaway screenshots written by the UI guards
docs/screenshots/_*.png
